WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
A thin beam of charged particles
races in a straight line.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.880
Switch on a magnetic
field across its path,

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.700
and the beam swerves.

4
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.850
A current is moving charge, so each
particle crossing the field feels a magnetic

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.030
force.

6
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.350
A magnet can steer the beam.

7
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.580
But can it also make
the particles go faster?

8
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.700
In this mission, you'll calculate
the force on a single moving charge,

9
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:29.280
such as an electron crossing
a field of 0.20 tesla.

10
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.310
Then you'll work out
which way that force acts,

11
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.190
for positive and negative charges alike.

12
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.860
Your mission: find out whether a magnetic
field can also make the particles go

13
00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.750
faster.
